      "description": "Most heat (often ~ 60–70 %) is absorbed in the radiant section, where the flue gas is hottest (bridge-wall temperature often ~ 700–900 °C). The convection section recovers more heat from the cooler gas; the stack temperature sets the main efficiency loss. Tube metal temperature and heat flux limit the firing rate (API 560 / API 530).",
